    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "Build is green. Here's what I implemented to satisfy the `age-band` specification.\n\n## Change\n\n`POST /api/owners` now accepts an optional ISO `birthDate`; the owner's derived `ageBand` (`MINOR` / `ADULT` / `SENIOR`) is returned, computed as the owner's age **at their `registrationDate`**.\n\n## Files touched\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `birthDate` (`format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema, and a read-only `ageBand` enum (`MINOR`/`ADULT`/`SENIOR`) to the `Owner` schema. These regenerate the `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` at build time.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added the persisted `birthDate` field (`birth_date DATE` column) with getter/setter. MapStruct now carries `birthDate` request\u2192entity\u2192response by name, matching the existing `registrationDate` handling.\n\n3. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added an `ageBand(Owner)` derivation wired via `@Mapping(target = \"ageBand\", ...)`. It returns `null` when no `birthDate` is present (field then absent from the response); otherwise `Period.between(birthDate, registrationDate).getYears()` bands as `<18 \u2192 MINOR`, `18\u201364 \u2192 ADULT`, `\u226565 \u2192 SENIOR`. It falls back to the current date only for legacy owners lacking a `registrationDate`.\n\n4. **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres` `schema.sql`) \u2014 added the `birth_date DATE` column to the `owners` table.\n\n5. **`hsqldb/data.sql`** \u2014 the seed rows use positional `INSERT ... VALUES`, so I added the matching `NULL` for the new column to the 10 owner rows (the other DBs' seeds use explicit column lists and needed no change).\n\nThe `AcceptanceTest.coreDerivesAgeBand` test (birthDate `1990-01-01` \u2192 `ADULT` at today's registration date) and the rest of the suite pass \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\nNote: because `birthDate` lives on the shared `OwnerFields` schema, it is also echoed back on reads. The spec only requires `ageBand` in the response and doesn't mention hiding `birthDate`, so I left it visible (consistent with how `registrationDate` is handled). If you'd prefer `birthDate` be write-only, that's a one-line `writeOnly: true` addition \u2014 let me know.",
